 "after": {
  "answer": "The build cylinder appears to fit into the **Main Platform**: the cylinder drawing gives a corrected Ø262,0 j7 diameter, and the Main Platform drawing gives a Ø262 H8 bore. That suggests a transition fit, but it is an inferred match—not a stated connection. [D-023.p1.vision.c06.C-001] [D-003.p1.vision.c15]\n\nThe Z-axis diagram also says the cylinder registers on the **Print Platform**; its top edge carries the platform registration surfaces. [Zaxis_legend.l03] [Zaxis_legend.l04]\n\nCaution: another cylinder callout, “Ø264,0 H7 +0,026 / -0,026,” failed the ISO 286 check because an H7 bore should have a lower deviation of 0; the reading or feature grouping is probably wrong, so it is not used to infer a fit. [D-023.p1.vision.c07]",
